      "side": 1,
      "message": "###  Global State for Device Handle (`iapcontrol.cc`)\n\n**Issue:** `g_devHandelPtr` is defined as a namespace-level global variable (`LibusbDeviceHandlePtr g_devHandelPtr;`). **Impact:** This breaks encapsulation and makes the `iapcontrol` class fundamentally unsafe to instantiate more than once. If multiple `iapcontrol` objects are created, they will silently overwrite and clobber each other\u0027s USB handles. **Recommendation:** Move `g_devHandelPtr` to be a private class member of `iapcontrol` (e.g., `m_devHandlePtr`).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 86,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 86,
