      "side": 1,
      "message": "### CLI Parsing Fragility (`iaptool.cc`)\n\n**Issue:** `CommandLineManager` uses `strtol(buff[i + 1], nullptr, 16)` without checking if the conversion actually succeeded. Furthermore, if a flag is passed without a corresponding value at the end of the argument list, the loop bounds check (`i + 1 \u003c buff.size()`) protects it from a crash, but it silently ignores the flag. \n**Impact:** Passing invalid hex strings (e.g., `-V GXYZ`) results in `0` without warning the user. \n**Recommendation:** Use `std::strtol` and check the `endptr` to ensure successful parsing.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 55,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d8fed2004e8fb6edb9673b6e6e59537ac06bc029",
